  #line-at(110.78pt, 429.07pt, ". Many such utilities involve droplet formation ")
  #line-at(54pt, 440.59pt, "and/or filament stretching within MF. Therefore, under- ")
  #line-at(54pt, 451.99pt, "standing the rheology of FF during magnetically induced ")
  #line-at(54pt, 463.51pt, "extensional flows holds crucial importance. ")
  #line-at(63.84pt, 484.51pt, "Rheological characterization typically comprises shear and ")
  #line-at(54pt, 495.91pt, "extensional rheology (ER). Shear rheology probes the re- ")
  #line-at(54pt, 507.43pt, "sponse of a fluid to tangential deformation, and has been used ")
  #line-at(54pt, 518.95pt, "widely for FF, particularly to quantify magnetoviscous effects ")
  #line-at(326.93pt, 268.01pt, "Extensional behavior of FF develops further complexi- ")
  #line-at(316.97pt, 279.53pt, "ties in a MF, as magnetic interactions promote nanoparticle- ")
  #line-at(316.97pt, 291.05pt, "chain-formation and anisotropic structures, leading to non- ")
  #line-at(316.97pt, 302.57pt, "Newtonian behavior, and altering the stresses borne of stretch- ")
  #line-at(316.97pt, 313.97pt, "ing. Despite a body of literature on magnetically induced ")
  #line-at(316.97pt, 325.49pt, "changes in shear rheology, experimental studies of magneto- ")
  #line-at(316.97pt, 337.01pt, "ER are still number in few. Early research probed magnetic ")
  #line-at(316.97pt, 348.53pt, "colloids using extensional flows, and showed elongational ")
  #line-at(316.97pt, 360.05pt, "viscosity as strongly sensitive to MF strength")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(510.82pt, 355.49pt, "23")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(517.3pt, 360.05pt, ". Research ")
  #line-at(316.97pt, 371.57pt, "has remained concentrated to configurations where the MF ")
  #line-at(316.97pt, 382.97pt, "is aligned with the primary deformation direction, and cap- ")
  #line-at(316.97pt, 394.49pt, "illary breakup extensional magneto-rheometry has been pro- ")
  #line-at(316.97pt, 406.01pt, "posed more recently to quantify magnetically induced exten- ")
  #line-at(316.97pt, 417.53pt, "sional stresses")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(374.71pt, 412.97pt, "24")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(381.19pt, 417.53pt, ". In most literature, MF are aligned with ei- ")
  #line-at(316.97pt, 429.07pt, "ther the direction of stretching, or with gravity. Additional ")
  #line-at(316.97pt, 440.59pt, "non-trivial physical mechanisms are introduced when trans- ")
  #line-at(316.97pt, 451.99pt, "verse magnetic stresses interact with elongational deforma- ")
  #line-at(316.97pt, 463.51pt, "tion and with the changing microstructure in extensional flows ")
  #line-at(316.97pt, 475.03pt, "under a transversely applied MF. Such configurations remain ")
  #line-at(316.97pt, 486.55pt, "scarcely explored in experiments, despite their practical sig- ")
  #line-at(316.97pt, 498.07pt, "nificance. ")
