  #line-at(384.55pt, 469.15pt, "for the three FF concentrations. ")
  #line-at(54pt, 504.43pt, "the strong magnetic pull disrupts or rearranges the chains dur- ")
  #line-at(54pt, 515.95pt, "ing rapid stretching beyond a critical MF strength, preventing ")
  #line-at(54pt, 527.47pt, "additional elastic stress accumulation. In precis, the slope of ")
  #line-at(54pt, 538.87pt, "the fitting curves captures the competition between capillar- ")
  #line-at(54pt, 550.39pt, "ity, magnetism-induced-elasticity, and microstructural stabil- ")
  #line-at(54pt, 561.91pt, "ity across a range of MF strengths, and offers a compact, yet ")
  #line-at(54pt, 573.43pt, "physically consistent measure of the balance between exten- ")
  #line-at(54pt, 584.95pt, "sional thinning and thickening. ")
  #line-at(63.96pt, 606.82pt, "Figure 7 summarizes the variant filament thinning man- ")
  #line-at(54pt, 618.22pt, "nerisms as function of MF strength and MNP concentration; ")
  #line-at(54pt, 629.74pt, "broadly classified into three regimes. In ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(220.25pt, 629.74pt, "Regime I")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(256.73pt, 629.74pt, ", pinch-off ")
  #line-at(54pt, 641.14pt, "occurs at the bottom of the filament, resembling conventional ")
  #line-at(54pt, 652.66pt, "capillary breakup. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(131.42pt, 652.66pt, "Regime II ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(174.5pt, 652.66pt, "is characterized by the appear- ")
  #line-at(54pt, 664.18pt, "ance of BOAS, arising from the competition between capillary ")
  #line-at(54pt, 675.7pt, "forces and magneto-elastic stresses induced by field-driven ")
  #line-at(54pt, 687.22pt, "MNP chaining, suppressing uniform thinning and promoting ")
  #line-at(54pt, 698.736pt, "bead formation. In ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(134.54pt, 698.736pt, "Regime III")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(178.22pt, 698.736pt, ", corresponding to high MNP ")
  #line-at(54pt, 710.136pt, "concentration and strong MF, a long filament forms but pinch- ")
  #line-at(54pt, 721.656pt, "off shifts toward the parent droplet-end. Here, the filament ")
  #line-at(316.97pt, 504.43pt, "segment attached to the detaching drop is strongly stiffened ")
  #line-at(316.97pt, 515.95pt, "by magneto-elastic stresses, while weaker magnetic resistance ")
  #line-at(316.97pt, 527.47pt, "near the parent drop permits capillary forces to dominate, ini- ")
  #line-at(316.97pt, 538.87pt, "tiating filament breakup at the top. ")
  #line-at(326.93pt, 560.83pt, "To infer„ we experimentally investigate filament thin- ")
  #line-at(316.97pt, 572.35pt, "ning and pinch-off in FF exposed to a transverse MF. The ")
  #line-at(316.97pt, 583.87pt, "findings show that a tunable magneto-elastic response, that ")
  #line-at(316.97pt, 595.3pt, "significantly alters extensional flow dynamics, is introduced ")
  #line-at(316.97pt, 606.82pt, "by MF-induced MNP chaining. Within MF, the FF exhibit ")
  #line-at(316.97pt, 618.34pt, "extensional thickening, BOAS formation, and field-dependent ")
  #line-at(316.97pt, 629.86pt, "extensional relaxation times, despite their effective behavior ")
  #line-at(316.97pt, 641.38pt, "as Newtonian liquids at MF=0 T. A regime map delineates ")
  #line-at(316.97pt, 652.78pt, "different breakup modes, such as a shift to top-pinch-off at ")
  #line-at(316.97pt, 664.3pt, "high MF strengths and MNP concentrations; controlled by the ")
  #line-at(316.97pt, 675.82pt, "competition between capillary and magneto-elastic stresses. ")
  #line-at(316.97pt, 687.34pt, "Our results show that transverse MF can be a useful control ")
  #line-at(316.97pt, 698.856pt, "parameter for extensional rheology of FF. ")
  #set text(font: "Century", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(509.14pt, 382.97pt, "10 wt ")
